<!doctype html>
<html lang="en"><head><meta charset="utf-8"><meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width,initial-scale=1">
<title>sub-{{ report.participant_id }} · BPlus Multimodal Research Report</title>
<style>
:root{--navy:#17365d;--blue:#2f75b5;--bg:#f4f7fb;--card:#fff;--text:#1f2d3d;--muted:#607080;--pass:#2e7d32;--warn:#b26a00;--fail:#b71c1c;--line:#d9e2ef}
*{box-sizing:border-box}body{margin:0;overflow-x:hidden;font-family:-apple-system,BlinkMacSystemFont,"Segoe UI","PingFang SC","Noto Sans CJK SC",Arial,sans-serif;background:var(--bg);color:var(--text)}
.page{width:1180px;max-width:calc(100vw - 32px);margin:24px auto;padding:0 0 40px}.hero{background:linear-gradient(135deg,var(--navy),#275f95);color:#fff;padding:28px;border-radius:18px;box-shadow:0 8px 28px rgba(0,0,0,.12)}
.hero h1{margin:0 0 8px;font-size:28px}.hero .meta{opacity:.9}.notice{margin-top:14px;background:#fff4d7;color:#664d03;padding:12px 14px;border-radius:10px;font-weight:600}
.grid{display:block;margin-top:16px}.report-row{display:flex;gap:16px;align-items:stretch;margin-bottom:16px}.card{background:var(--card);border:1px solid var(--line);border-radius:14px;padding:18px;box-shadow:0 2px 8px rgba(23,54,93,.04);min-width:0;overflow:hidden;display:flex;flex-direction:column}
.row-top>.card{flex:1 1 0}.w-50{flex:1 1 50%}.w-67{flex:2 1 0}.w-33{flex:1 1 0}.w-100{flex:1 1 100%}.card h2{min-height:32px;display:flex;align-items:center;flex-wrap:wrap;gap:8px;margin:0 0 12px;font-size:18px;color:var(--navy)}
.metric{font-size:28px;font-weight:700;color:var(--navy)}.unit,.muted{color:var(--muted)}.small{font-size:12px}.bar{height:10px;background:#e8edf4;border-radius:8px;overflow:hidden}.bar i{display:block;height:100%;background:var(--blue)}
.badge{display:inline-block;border-radius:999px;padding:5px 10px;font-size:12px;font-weight:700}.PASS{background:#e8f5e9;color:var(--pass)}.WARN{background:#fff3e0;color:var(--warn)}.FAIL{background:#ffebee;color:var(--fail)}
.task{border-left:4px solid var(--blue)}.task-desc{min-height:46px;margin:2px 0 10px;color:#34495e;line-height:1.8}.result-table{width:100%;table-layout:fixed;border-collapse:collapse;margin-top:10px}.result-table th,.result-table td{min-width:0;padding:10px;border-bottom:1px solid var(--line);vertical-align:top;text-align:left;line-height:1.55;white-space:normal;overflow-wrap:anywhere;word-break:break-word}.result-table th{background:#f7f9fc;color:#43546a;font-size:13px}.result-table th:nth-child(1){width:24%}.result-table th:nth-child(2){width:16%}.result-table th:nth-child(3){width:20%}.result-table th:nth-child(4){width:40%}.result-table td:first-child{font-weight:700;color:var(--navy)}.result-table td:nth-child(2){font-weight:700}
.state-label{display:block;width:100%;max-width:100%;padding:4px 8px;border-radius:9px;font-size:12px;font-weight:700;line-height:1.45;white-space:normal;overflow-wrap:anywhere;word-break:break-word}.state-response{background:#edf7ff;color:#1769aa}.state-warn{background:#fff3e0;color:#a15c00}.state-pending{background:#f1f3f5;color:#6b7280}.compact-summary{margin-top:auto;padding:10px 12px;border-radius:10px;background:#f4f8fd;border-left:4px solid var(--blue);font-size:13px;color:#34495e;line-height:1.65;overflow-wrap:anywhere}.compact-summary.warn{background:#fff7e8;border-left-color:var(--warn)}
.overall-state{padding:14px 16px;border-radius:12px;background:#edf5ff;border-left:4px solid var(--blue)}.overall-state .state-title{font-size:16px;font-weight:800;color:var(--navy)}.section-note{margin-top:10px;padding:10px 12px;background:#f7f9fc;border-radius:9px;color:#455668;font-size:13px}.footer{margin-top:18px;color:#6b7785;font-size:12px;line-height:1.6}
@media(max-width:1100px){.page{width:auto;max-width:none;margin:12px;padding:0}.report-row{display:block;margin-bottom:0}.report-row>.card{width:100%;margin-bottom:14px}.task-desc{min-height:0}}
@media(max-width:680px){.page{margin:0;padding:10px}.card{padding:14px}.result-table th,.result-table td{padding:8px 6px;font-size:12px}.result-table th:nth-child(1){width:23%}.result-table th:nth-child(2){width:17%}.result-table th:nth-child(3){width:23%}.result-table th:nth-child(4){width:37%}}
@media print{body{background:#fff}.page{width:auto;max-width:none;margin:0;padding:0}.report-row{display:block;margin-bottom:0}.report-row>.card{width:100%;margin-bottom:10px;break-inside:avoid}.card,.hero{box-shadow:none}.hero{border-radius:0}.result-table th,.result-table td{overflow-wrap:anywhere;word-break:break-word}}
</style></head><body><main class="page">
<section class="hero"><h1>BPlus Youth Multimodal Research Report</h1><div class="meta">Participant: sub-{{ report.participant_id }} · Session: ses-{{ report.session_id }} · Date: {{ report.date }} · Report version: {{ report.report_version }} · {{ "Software Simulation Validation" if report.stage == "SIMULATION" else ("Reviewed Research Version" if report.stage == "REVIEWED" else "Experiment Complete — Analysis Pending") }}</div><div class="notice">{{ report.notice }}</div></section>
<div class="grid"><div class="report-row row-top">
<section class="card"><h2>Overall Data Quality</h2><span class="badge {{ report.overall_qc }}">{{ report.overall_qc }}</span><p class="muted small">The quality grade describes data reliability only; it does not indicate whether brain function is good or poor.</p></section>
<section class="card"><h2>Task Modules with Interpretable Results</h2><div class="metric">{{ report.completed_modules }}<span class="unit"> / {{ report.total_modules }} ({{ report.completion_percent }}%)</span></div><div class="bar"><i style="width:{{ report.completion_percent }}%"></i></div><div class="section-note">This is not file-import progress; only modules with quantitative metrics that passed the corresponding QC are counted.</div></section>
<section class="card"><h2>Result Confidence</h2><div class="metric" style="font-size:24px">{{ report.confidence }}</div><p class="muted small">Indicates how strongly the current data support the research result, not diagnostic confidence.</p></section></div>
{% for pair in report.modules|batch(2, none) %}<div class="report-row">{% for module in pair if module %}<section class="card task {{ module.width }}"><h2>{{ module.title }} <span class="badge {{ module.badge_class }}">{{ module.qc }}</span></h2><p class="task-desc">{{ module.description }}</p><table class="result-table"><tr><th>Measure</th><th>Current Result</th><th>Current Status</th><th>Brief Explanation</th></tr>{% for row in module.rows %}<tr><td>{{ row.name }}</td><td>{{ row.display_value }}</td><td><span class="state-label {{ row.state_class }}">{{ row.state }}</span></td><td>{{ row.description }}</td></tr>{% endfor %}</table><div class="compact-summary{% if module.qc == 'WARN' %} warn{% endif %}">Integrated result: {{ module.summary }}</div></section>{% endfor %}</div>{% endfor %}
{% set module = report.clinical_module %}<div class="report-row"><section class="card task w-100"><h2>{{ module.title }} <span class="badge {{ module.badge_class }}">{{ module.qc }}</span></h2><p class="task-desc">{{ module.description }}</p><table class="result-table"><tr><th>Measure</th><th>Current Result</th><th>Current Status</th><th>Brief Explanation</th></tr>{% for row in module.rows %}<tr><td>{{ row.name }}</td><td>{{ row.display_value }}</td><td><span class="state-label {{ row.state_class }}">{{ row.state }}</span></td><td>{{ row.description }}</td></tr>{% endfor %}</table><div class="compact-summary{% if module.qc == 'WARN' %} warn{% endif %}">Integrated result: {{ module.summary }}</div></section></div>
<div class="report-row"><section class="card w-100"><h2>Integrated Narrative Result</h2><div class="overall-state"><div class="state-title">Overall status: {{ "The software simulation loop is complete; this must not be used as a real participant result." if report.stage == "SIMULATION" else ("The current result has completed researcher review." if report.stage == "REVIEWED" else "The experimental tasks are complete; some multimodal measures still require analysis and review.") }}</div><p>{{ report.overall_summary }}</p></div></section></div>
<div class="report-row"><section class="card w-100"><h2>How the Current Response Status Is Derived</h2><p>{{ report.interpretation_basis }}</p><div class="section-note">Current response status is derived from the value in the same row and describes response direction, magnitude, or timing within that task. It is not a disease judgment and cannot replace age-matched norms, repeated measurement, questionnaires, or clinical interviews.</div></section></div>
<div class="report-row"><section class="card w-100"><h2>Data Quality Details</h2><table class="result-table"><tr><th>Measure</th><th>Current Result</th><th>Current Status</th><th>Brief Explanation</th></tr>{% for row in report.quality_rows %}<tr><td>{{ row.name }}</td><td>{{ row.value }}</td><td>{{ row.state }}</td><td>{{ row.description }}</td></tr>{% endfor %}</table></section></div>
<div class="report-row"><section class="card w-100"><h2>Researcher Method Record · Data Preprocessing</h2><div class="section-note">The table distinguishes methods actually executed in this run from publication-level steps that have not been implemented. Planned methods must not be reported as completed methods.</div><table class="result-table"><tr><th>Data Type</th><th>Execution Status</th><th>Actually Executed</th><th>Not Executed / Interpretation Boundary</th></tr>{% for row in report.preprocessing_methods %}<tr><td>{{ row.modality }}</td><td>{{ row.status }}</td><td>{{ row.executed }}</td><td>{{ row.not_executed }} {{ row.scope }}</td></tr>{% endfor %}</table></section></div>
{% set model = report.modeling_status %}<div class="report-row"><section class="card w-100"><h2>Researcher Method Record · Modeling and Validation</h2><div class="overall-state"><div class="state-title">Model status: {{ model.status or "NOT TRAINED / NOT VALIDATED" }}</div><p>{{ model.current_output }}</p></div><table class="result-table"><tr><th>Stage</th><th>Current Status</th><th>Planned Method</th><th>Activation Requirements</th></tr><tr><td>Statistical analysis</td><td>Awaiting cohort data</td><td>{{ model.planned_primary_analysis }}</td><td rowspan="2">{% for item in model.required_before_activation %}{{ loop.index }}. {{ item }}{% if not loop.last %}<br>{% endif %}{% endfor %}</td></tr><tr><td>Predictive model</td><td>{{ model.status }}</td><td>{{ model.planned_prediction }}</td></tr></table></section></div>
<div class="report-row"><section class="card w-100"><h2>Interpretation Boundaries</h2><ul><li>This report does not output a depression probability, normal/abnormal brain-function label, or diagnosis.</li><li>A single EEG/fNIRS measure is not directly equivalent to good or poor function and must be interpreted with behavior and data quality.</li><li>Age-referenced position should only be considered after establishing age-matched references and completing independent validation.</li></ul><div class="section-note">The system does not infer conclusions from demonstration or missing data; pending measures are explicitly reported as insufficient data.</div></section></div>
<div class="report-row"><section class="card w-100"><h2>Methods and Evidence Basis</h2><ol>{% for reference in report.evidence_references %}<li>{{ reference }}</li>{% endfor %}</ol><div class="section-note">The cited papers support the research constructs represented by the measures and standard reporting methods. Labels such as marked, moderate, or weak remain project rules awaiting pilot calibration and are not clinical cutoffs supplied by those papers.</div></section></div></div>
<footer class="footer">Report version: {{ report.report_version }} · Method version: {{ report.method_version }}<br>Clinical interpretation must be completed by a clinical member of the research team using interviews, scales, and medical history.</footer>
</main></body></html>
